  "body": "Found by the QA swarm round 2 (#2582), brief q04 (sign plate on a Tormach 24R), CamCraft **v0.25.0** Linux x86_64 release; reproduced by hand.\n\n## What happens\n\nThe Tormach 24R machine file states no coolants. A user who sets an operation's coolant to **Off** (the right choice on a dry router) cannot post:\n\n```\npost: post blocked - 1 warning(s): operation F: asks off coolant, but this post script does not declare coolantModes (it does not read PARAM Coolant) - set the operation's coolant to Flood or use a post that reads it\n```\n\nSet back to **Flood**, the same program posts (65 lines) with no M7/M8/M9 at all, because tormach.cps treats an unstated coolant list as silent. So the refused setting and the accepted one give the same G-code, and the user is told to pick Flood on a machine without coolant. `verify` says `ok: true` before the post refuses.\n\nRepro (MCP): `import_model` any part, `load_machine {\"builtin\": \"Tormach 24R\"}`, `fit_stock`, `add_tool {\"catalog\": \"Router up-cut 6 mm\"}`, `add_operation {\"kind\": \"face\", ...}`, `set_operation_coolant {\"coolant\": \"off\"}`, `generate`, `post {\"post\": \"Tormach PathPilot\", ...}`.\n\n## Expected\n\nOn a machine whose coolant list is empty (or that states no Flood), Off posts: it writes no coolant word, which is what the post writes for Flood there anyway. Related but different: #3124 (hobby router files start new operations on Flood).\n\n## Repro files\n\n[q04-vcarve-sign-posted-5ops.camproj](https://github.com/mkinney/Camcraft/blob/qa-artifacts/qa/round2-20261122/q04-vcarve-sign/q04-vcarve-sign-posted-5ops.camproj), [REPORT.md](https://github.com/mkinney/Camcraft/blob/qa-artifacts/qa/round2-20261122/q04-vcarve-sign/REPORT.md) problem 10.\n\nDone means: a Tormach 24R operation with Coolant Off posts through Tormach PathPilot with no coolant word (pinned by a post test), and Flood on a machine with no coolant list either still posts silently or says so in the post notes.\n",
